OL,3,A'Public have heard enough from Russell
OL,4,ABrand', says PM's spokesman
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe public "have heard enough" from
OL,7,FRussell Brand, the prime minister's
OL,8,Fofficial spokesperson has said, after
OL,9,Fthe government attempted to have a
OL,10,FYouTube video featuring a message from
OL,11,Fthe jailed comedian taken down.
OL,13,FThe site's owner Google refused a
OL,14,Fgovernment request to remove the clip
OL,15,Fposted by Brand's wife in which he
OL,16,Fclaims his innocence, Whitehall sources
OL,17,Fhave told the BBC.
OL,19,FBrand was sentenced to 10-and-a-half
OL,20,Fyears in prison after being convicted
OL,21,Fof rape and three counts of sexual
OL,22,Fassault.
OL,23,APub: 18-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
